  "description": "On 2026\u201106\u201115 at 12:34:56\u202fUTC the CloudFront distribution **d111111abcdef8.cloudfront.net** received a **GET** request over **https** (using **HTTP/2**) from client IP **203.0.113.42** (also seen in the X\u2011Forwarded\u2011For header). The request targeted the object **/images/logo.png** with the query string **id=10&sort=asc**, and carried a cookie of **sessionid=abc123; theme=light**. The referer was **https://example.com/home**, and the client identified itself with the user\u2011agent string **Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/124.0.0.0 Safari/537.36**. The host header sent was **d111111abcdef8.cloudfront.net**.\n\nThe edge server handling the request was **LAX53**, and the request was logged with the identifier **a1b2c3d4-5678-90ab-cdef-1234567890ab**. Both the edge result type and the edge response result type were recorded as **Miss**. The client transferred **4523** bytes (csBytes) and received **9876** bytes (scBytes) in response, with an HTTP status code of **200**. The TLS handshake used the cipher **ECDHE-RSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256** over **TLSv1.2**, and the entire transaction took **0.124** seconds. Field\u2011level encryption was applied (fleEncryptedFields\u202f=\u202fYES) and its status was reported as **OK**.",
